>>>

<<<
 the -al word is better suited to the most general sense of all, ‘ concerned with proportion’, & the -ate word to the particular sense ‘ analogous in quantity to’, but
===
 the *-al* word is better suited to the most general sense of all, ' concerned with proportion', & the *-ate* word to the particular sense ' analogous in quantity *to*', but
>>>

<<<
 -al & -ate are both so fully in possession of the most usual sense ‘in proportion’ or ‘in due proportion’ that it is useless to think of confining it to either.
===
 *-al* & *-ate* are both so fully in possession of the most usual sense ' in proportion ' or 'in due proportion' that it is useless to think of confining it to either.
>>>

