<<<
propose. 1. P. makes -sable; see Mure E. 2. The Insurance Commissioners proposed to be appointed will give their whole time to the work of the Commission. P. is one of the verbs liable to be used in tbis ungainly construction, for which see DOUBLE PASSIVES.
===
**propose.** 1. *P.* makes *-sable*; see ^^MUTE E^^. 2. *The Insurance Commissioners* proposed to be appointed *will give their whole time to the work of the Commission.* *P.* is one of the verbs liable to be used in this ungainly construction, for which see ^^DOUBLE PASSIVES^^.
>>>

